00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.429 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  this  celebratory rally in havana is a far cry  from angry protests that have gripped  this caribbean nation  performing cuban salsa and waving flags  thousands of people showed support  for president miguel diaz-canel he says  protests against cuba's economic decline  were based on false narratives they are  encouraging and glorifying disrespect  and destruction of property  threats and harassments of citizens and  families  right now what the world is seeing from  cuba is a lie  raul castro joined the president who he  had handed power to  in 2019. he and his brother the late  fidel castro  had led the cuban revolution more than  six decades ago  pandemic or no pandemic we have to  defend this revolution  we have to defend what is ours  in the words of miguel diaz-canel he  made it clear to the whole world  that this revolution will not be  overthrown  a week ago a wave of protests hit 40  cuban cities  the biggest in decades  people are calling for liberty freedom  and down with the dictatorship  they galvanized in their thousands over  shortages of goods  and the government's handling of a surge  in covert 19 infections  scores of people were arrested  [Applause]  almost 2 000 kilometers north in  washington dc  protesters showed solidarity outside the  cuban embassy  my grandmother left in 1970 without the  expectation of going back  and because of the dictatorship in cuba  we have not been afforded that  opportunity  those calls were echoed among the large  cuban american population in florida  u.s president joe biden called cuba a  failed state  and showed no sign of lifting economic  sanctions  the country now seems divided between  two camps  those who blame the government on  widespread shortages of food  and medicine and those who don't want to  lose their socialist revolution  they blame 60 years of crippling  sanctions for their economic woes  al jazeera

